{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rapid elasticity rapid elasticity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md","fileName":"Rapid Elasticity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Rapid Elasticity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Computing Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Computing Foundations","Horizontal Scalability","Resource Pooling","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rapid elasticity rapid elasticity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md","fileName":"Rapid Elasticity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Rapid Elasticity","heading":"Rapid Elasticity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Rapid elasticity is the ability to add resources when demand rises and release them when demand falls. It uses [[Horizontal Scalability]] in both directions so that capacity can follow a changing workload instead of remaining fixed at its anticipated peak.\n\nElasticity depends on [[Resource Pooling]], automation, and sufficiently fast provisioning. It can protect service availability during a surge and reduce idle capacity afterward, but it does not remove the need to measure workload behavior or set safe scaling rules.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Computing Foundations","Horizontal Scalability","Resource Pooling","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Rapid Elasticity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","